# BMW X5 E53 five-door SUV, 1999-2006.
#
# The first X5: the E39-based 'Sports Activity Vehicle' with the tall body,
# the split tailgate, the short overhangs and the 4.4i V8 or 3.0d six. UK
# sales began in 2000.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMW_X5_(E53)
#
# Dimensions 4.666 x 1.872 x 1.707-1.760 m, wheelbase 2.819 m.
#
# Shape reference: NO true level side profile exists. Image 1 is the most
# side-on view (a 3.0d with aftermarket wheels); the front and rear
# three-quarters show the lamps, split tailgate and bumpers. The limitation
# is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (c), provisional; no UK chart was verified. Black, silver,
# green and blue are plain names. Weights 18, 16, 14, 12, total 60,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 200 km/h. Comfort 90/465, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 90. Class 3.
# Dates are road presence: 2000 intro, retires staggered 2020-2023.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bmw-x5-e53.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/bmw-x5-e53.dae. References:
# citycars/references/bmw-x5-e53/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the amber front indicators, lower cladding and split-
# tailgate seam are understated; the aftermarket alloys in image 1 were not
# copied. At 128 px the tall body, short overhangs and split tailgate read as an
# E53 X5.


obj=citycar
name=BMWX5E53(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=18
intro_year=2000
intro_month=1
retire_year=2023
retire_month=6
speed=200
class=3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=90
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=465

